<title>UK: Strike delays Air India UK cargo one day.</title>
<headline>Strike delays Air India UK cargo one day.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air India said that cargo it planned to fly to India from London Heathrow airport on April 11 was delayed by 24 hours due due an Indian air traffic controllers' strike.</p>
<p>The strike began on Friday and was called off at around 1130 GMT on Saturday.</p>
<p>&quot;It did not cause any major disruptions for us,&quot; Air India's UK cargo manager Madhav Lokur told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;Only a couple of tonnes of cargo was affected and instead of Friday, it went on our flight the next day. Everything is now back to normal,&quot; he said. - Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel +44 171 542 7706 Fax +5017</p>
</text>
